WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:11.237 --> 01:13.114
♪ Yesterday ♪

01:14.365 --> 01:18.578
♪ All my troubles seemed so far away… ♪

01:18.661 --> 01:19.913
Oh goodness.

01:21.456 --> 01:23.374
It's all right. A poem can be simple.

01:24.125 --> 01:26.753
You just write down the things
you'd like to say.

01:26.836 --> 01:28.254
That's all there is to it.

01:28.338 --> 01:30.340
♪ Suddenly… ♪

01:30.423 --> 01:32.300
Ok-sim, make us food

01:32.383 --> 01:35.011
Look at me, give me food

01:35.095 --> 01:36.304
Hey, Mom

01:36.387 --> 01:37.931
Food, food, food

01:38.014 --> 01:40.850
Stop saying, "Ok-sim, make me food"

01:40.934 --> 01:44.104
I must have spent my whole life
Making food

01:45.230 --> 01:48.608
Think about the things
you've always wanted to say the most.

01:49.651 --> 01:53.029
"Respect Your Elders"
by Lee Byeong-seon.

01:54.239 --> 01:57.283
Eyes fading, ears fading too

01:57.784 --> 01:59.536
Sons and daughters

02:00.120 --> 02:02.413
My back is killing me

02:03.206 --> 02:05.792
Please come and visit me often

02:07.836 --> 02:10.713
Someone hasn't written a single word yet.

02:12.006 --> 02:14.801
Just write down
what you want to say the most.

02:15.969 --> 02:17.929
That's how you write a poem about life.

02:18.012 --> 02:22.809
♪ Oh, I believe in yesterday ♪

02:23.309 --> 02:27.397
♪ Why she had to go ♪

02:27.480 --> 02:31.860
♪ I don't know, she wouldn't say ♪

02:33.153 --> 02:37.240
♪ I said something wrong ♪

02:37.323 --> 02:38.741
♪ Now I long… ♪

02:38.825 --> 02:40.410
I didn't know back then

02:41.327 --> 02:43.329
that I'd ever reach the age of 70.

02:43.413 --> 02:44.873
♪ Yesterday… ♪

02:46.374 --> 02:49.711
♪ Love was such an easy game to play ♪

02:59.846 --> 03:01.723
I didn't know back then…

03:03.600 --> 03:05.685
…that what I'd want to say the most at 70

03:06.728 --> 03:09.564
is a word
I said more than any other, every day.

03:10.940 --> 03:11.983
Mom.

03:49.020 --> 03:49.938
Mom.

03:57.237 --> 03:58.613
Hey, Mom.

04:00.448 --> 04:01.783
Mom!

04:07.205 --> 04:08.289
Mom!

04:08.831 --> 04:10.083
Mom!

04:10.166 --> 04:11.209
Mom!

04:12.001 --> 04:14.212
Hey, Mom! Hey!

04:14.796 --> 04:17.173
Come out quickly, Mom! Hurry up!

04:17.257 --> 04:19.592
Why are you always
the last one to come out?

04:22.637 --> 04:24.138
Oh, come on!

04:24.222 --> 04:26.891
Are abalones more important
than your daughter?

04:27.642 --> 04:29.227
Why did you go back down?

04:29.310 --> 04:31.521
Are you doing it just to annoy me?

04:32.021 --> 04:34.399
Mom! Come on!

04:34.482 --> 04:36.818
There's green laver all over
the ocean floor in the spring.

04:36.901 --> 04:38.444
That greedy woman won't come out.

04:38.528 --> 04:40.905
Hey, Ae-sun, leave your mother alone.

04:40.989 --> 04:43.241
Instead, look at the color
of Mr. Yang's cheeks!

04:45.159 --> 04:46.953
It's just sunburn. I told you.

04:47.036 --> 04:50.123
Oh, something's burning all right,
young man. It's his little heart.

04:50.206 --> 04:52.041
Only Ae-sun can't see it!

04:53.376 --> 04:54.752
Can you imagine that?

04:54.836 --> 04:56.921
A haenyeo's daughter marrying
a fish merchant?

04:57.005 --> 04:59.382
All of Jeju would be out of business!

05:00.383 --> 05:02.093
You're so damn annoying!

05:06.014 --> 05:07.515
She's going over. Look.

05:08.558 --> 05:11.060
Did someone smack you or what?

05:11.144 --> 05:12.645
Why are your cheeks always red?

05:14.063 --> 05:16.190
She's turned him down again.

05:25.575 --> 05:28.995
My mom should have just given birth
to an abalone instead of me.

05:30.079 --> 05:31.247
Mr. Yang.

05:31.748 --> 05:34.375
There are two conches. Here.

05:35.001 --> 05:37.128
Get us a fair price
for them, all right?

05:37.795 --> 05:38.838
Yes, ma'am.

05:39.714 --> 05:42.342
Did you swim down the hall of
the Dragon King for that seaweed?

05:43.217 --> 05:46.054
It's not the sea
that kills haenyeo. It's greed.

05:46.137 --> 05:49.182
Greed is deadlier than the sea,
and that's a fact.

05:49.766 --> 05:52.643
By the way,
how is Grandma from Hallim doing?

05:53.227 --> 05:54.729
Her lungs won't ever recover.

05:54.812 --> 05:57.815
She can only make a living
from what we put in these bags,

05:57.899 --> 05:59.317
so let's keep her alive, eh?

05:59.984 --> 06:01.819
Is there only seaweed in this one?

06:02.445 --> 06:04.155
Mom wants at least a few abalones.

06:04.238 --> 06:05.656
There's a few there, see?

06:06.157 --> 06:08.034
Abalones are tiny in the spring.

06:08.618 --> 06:10.620
There's not much for them to eat.

06:13.039 --> 06:15.666
You may as well give
the whole thing away! Just take it all!

06:15.750 --> 06:17.627
There she goes again, losing her shit.

06:17.710 --> 06:19.253
Grandma from Hallim has three sons.

06:19.337 --> 06:21.506
Why are we the ones
to have to feed those hungry kids?

06:22.131 --> 06:25.343
I don't risk my life for them,
diving into that hellscape every day.

06:25.885 --> 06:27.804
I do it for my own children.

06:27.887 --> 06:30.723
I don't dive for abalones
to feed someone else's family.

06:31.557 --> 06:33.309
You think you're special, huh?

06:33.393 --> 06:35.144
Who taught you everything you know?

06:35.228 --> 06:37.563
Who do you owe for being able
to feed your children?

06:37.647 --> 06:41.025
My children depend on what I catch
to feed them. Same as you.

06:41.109 --> 06:43.569
We can't afford to be feeding
a sick grandma too.

06:43.653 --> 06:45.321
I'm not giving up my abalone.

06:45.822 --> 06:48.825
Just the thought infuriates me.
Make sure you count 'em.

06:48.908 --> 06:51.327
What do you think made her sick
in the first place?

06:51.828 --> 06:54.372
We'd do the same for you
if you were bedridden.

06:54.455 --> 06:56.040
I will never be bedridden.

06:56.124 --> 06:59.085
Haenyeo live and die together.
None of us can do it alone.

06:59.168 --> 07:02.880
Well, if you're all such saints,
what do you need the Dragon King for?

07:03.881 --> 07:06.175
I thought that new husband
would satisfy you,

07:06.259 --> 07:08.010
but you're just greedier than ever.

07:09.637 --> 07:11.305
How can you pamper that lazy man

07:11.389 --> 07:13.766
and think your abalones
are too good for sanggun?

07:13.850 --> 07:15.852
We were both poor as dirt
when we came here together.

07:15.935 --> 07:17.979
At least I remember who taught us to dive.

07:18.062 --> 07:20.481
If you can't respect what
Hallim Grandma did for us,

07:20.565 --> 07:22.650
you're worth less than a snailfish.

07:22.733 --> 07:25.778
If you're so much better than me,
why is your husband's face paralyzed?

07:26.696 --> 07:29.073
That was because he slept out in the cold!

07:29.157 --> 07:31.534
His face is paralyzed
because he barely eats.

07:31.617 --> 07:33.703
Huh? You gonna tell me I'm wrong?

07:33.786 --> 07:36.247
You don't get
to talk to me that way.

07:36.330 --> 07:37.707
You're no better than I am.

07:37.790 --> 07:40.376
At least I don't have children
with two different men!

07:40.460 --> 07:41.919
-Easy now.
-Gyeong-ja.

07:42.003 --> 07:44.505
-Enough.
-Here we go again.

07:45.298 --> 07:48.134
She always starts a fight
right before we go home.

07:56.350 --> 07:57.268
Wha-- Hey, what?

07:58.436 --> 07:59.395
What are you--

07:59.479 --> 08:02.857
Damn it. You damn brat.
What did you do that for? Shit!

08:02.940 --> 08:06.110
Ugh! You spilled my conches everywhere!
You damn menace!

08:06.652 --> 08:07.528
Damn it!

08:08.196 --> 08:10.990
Why the hell did I bring her with me
when I came here?

08:11.491 --> 08:14.368
-Oh, what a waste! They're ruined!
-Happens when you poke a puffer fish.

08:14.452 --> 08:17.997
When a woman is fighting to survive,
you stay out of her way.

08:18.623 --> 08:20.124
What a damn waste.

08:20.625 --> 08:23.628
Why don't you try kicking that leech
of a husband you keep at home

08:23.711 --> 08:25.713
instead of taking it out on my catch?

08:45.983 --> 08:48.402
You can't spare a second
for your daughter.

08:48.486 --> 08:51.072
I won a prize,
but you only care about those snails.

08:51.155 --> 08:52.698
What good does a poem do?

08:52.782 --> 08:55.368
Does writing a poem
bring home any abalones?

08:55.910 --> 08:57.370
Can't you just read it, Mom?

08:57.453 --> 08:59.539
It won second prize in school.

08:59.622 --> 09:01.207
Go and show your grandmother.

09:01.290 --> 09:03.251
The Oh family likes its scholars.

09:06.170 --> 09:09.298
Show it to her and… and then say,
"Please keep me in school."

09:09.799 --> 09:11.425
Grandma hates me.

09:12.093 --> 09:14.178
She says I remind her
more of you every day.

09:14.262 --> 09:16.681
That's why she can't stand
the sight of me.

09:16.764 --> 09:18.641
Go on to your own house for supper.

09:18.724 --> 09:20.810
I told them I'd eat with you.

09:20.893 --> 09:23.437
Go. Your stepdad's coming.

09:23.938 --> 09:25.147
Who cares, Mom?

09:25.231 --> 09:26.691
Can't I have dinner here?

09:26.774 --> 09:29.110
I want a conch
with the red seaweed you picked.

09:29.652 --> 09:32.947
A daughter of the Oh family
should eat at the Oh household.

09:33.030 --> 09:35.408
Uncle won't even give me a yellow croaker.

09:37.577 --> 09:38.703
What do you mean, he doesn't?

09:38.786 --> 09:41.747
He says having a girl around
who gets good grades and awards

09:41.831 --> 09:43.207
is stealing all his son's luck.

09:43.291 --> 09:46.544
He says it's my fault
Oh Jong-gu is at the bottom of his class.

09:47.295 --> 09:49.505
The yellow croaker
isn't even the worst part.

09:50.756 --> 09:52.883
It's how he treats me at the table.

09:52.967 --> 09:54.260
It's not fair.

09:54.343 --> 09:56.512
I'm so sad that I can hardly eat.

09:57.471 --> 09:58.598
Every time I'm there,

09:59.098 --> 10:00.349
I just get too choked up.

10:01.809 --> 10:04.061
Please, Mom,
can I just live here with you?

10:04.770 --> 10:05.605
Can I?

10:06.480 --> 10:07.732
Maybe someday?

10:10.151 --> 10:12.111
-Never, ever?
-What are you choked up for anyway?

10:12.194 --> 10:13.362
Did you do something wrong?

10:13.446 --> 10:16.115
How do you expect anyone to love you
acting like that?

10:17.825 --> 10:18.951
Go.

10:19.035 --> 10:19.869
Go!

10:19.952 --> 10:22.955
Learn how to defend yourself. Figure out
some way to make them love you.

10:23.039 --> 10:26.042
Well, what do you know?
Sun-ae is here again.

10:26.125 --> 10:27.376
Ae-sun, not Sun-ae!

10:27.460 --> 10:28.586
Are you an idiot?

10:29.086 --> 10:30.296
Ae-sun, right.

10:30.379 --> 10:32.006
Staying for dinner?

10:32.673 --> 10:34.342
No, I'm going home.

10:48.814 --> 10:50.316
That little brat.

10:56.113 --> 10:57.531
Daddy. Have some water.

10:57.615 --> 10:59.283
Thanks.

10:59.367 --> 11:01.619
She's always such a pain in the ass.

11:03.579 --> 11:05.665
Cigarettes can kill you, Mom.

11:06.540 --> 11:09.585
Haenyeo rely on their lungs.
You must have a death wish.

11:17.927 --> 11:20.554
Why don't you just let her live with us?

11:21.263 --> 11:23.808
For one thing,
she'd be much better off here.

11:23.891 --> 11:25.017
Surely you see that.

11:26.560 --> 11:29.522
You do nothing for your
own family, so mind your own business.

11:29.605 --> 11:32.149
We don't have the money
or space to raise her.

11:32.233 --> 11:34.652
This tiny hut we rent
is too small as it is.

11:34.735 --> 11:37.697
You blame a child for wanting
to feel her mother's embrace?

11:37.780 --> 11:41.659
Why do you care?
You prefer her to a cow.

11:41.742 --> 11:43.994
You want her to look after
her half-siblings?

11:44.495 --> 11:46.372
She'll always be family to you.

11:47.415 --> 11:51.335
Look, the only reason we're living here
is so you can be close to her.

11:51.419 --> 11:54.630
She's over practically every day
whenever she has the chance.

11:55.506 --> 11:59.760
She can't wait to live here with you,
but you insist on keeping her there.

11:59.844 --> 12:02.096
You're just setting her up for heartache.

12:02.179 --> 12:05.599
The Oh family has money. At least there,
she'll get a proper education.

12:05.683 --> 12:09.186
What's the point of letting a girl get
an education? It'll just frustrate her.

12:09.812 --> 12:11.272
Oh!

12:11.355 --> 12:14.817
Don't haenyeo start learning
how to dive when they're teenagers?

12:14.900 --> 12:16.736
Would you say that about
your own daughter?

12:16.819 --> 12:18.863
Is that the kind of life you want for her?

12:23.659 --> 12:26.454
You damn island women
will pick a fight over anything.

12:27.455 --> 12:28.956
I will never let her dive.

12:29.457 --> 12:31.917
You're better off being born a cow
than a haenyeo.

12:32.418 --> 12:34.879
I slave away every day for nothing!

12:34.962 --> 12:37.214
It's unbelievable
what we're expected to endure.

12:37.298 --> 12:39.717
What good would living here do her anyway?

12:40.301 --> 12:42.720
She's too soft.
She'll end up being your maid.

12:43.304 --> 12:44.555
Guess I'll throw this out, then.

12:46.766 --> 12:48.726
Reading it would just break your heart.

12:50.019 --> 12:51.729
Stop, you're crumpling it!

12:51.812 --> 12:54.690
That's no way to treat a winner.
It won second place.

12:57.818 --> 12:58.819
There, there.

13:00.112 --> 13:02.281
I mean it.
You're better off not reading it.

13:16.003 --> 13:17.463
GYONGGI NOODLE

13:24.804 --> 13:27.223
This is an "F," kid.
"F" as in you're a fool.

13:45.282 --> 13:47.368
That kid must have a death wish too.

13:55.626 --> 13:56.961
I only bought five.

13:57.545 --> 13:58.963
There's an extra one for free.

13:59.547 --> 14:00.673
Did your mom say that?

14:04.093 --> 14:05.094
Well, did she?

14:06.095 --> 14:09.515
You have six people in your family,
but for some reason, you only buy five.

14:09.598 --> 14:11.934
Think you're rich enough
to give 'em away, is that it?

14:12.017 --> 14:13.477
Mind your own business.

14:15.479 --> 14:17.022
He's so annoying.

14:17.648 --> 14:18.691
Yi-suk.

14:18.774 --> 14:19.859
-Huh?
-Here.

14:19.942 --> 14:20.818
Yeah?

14:22.736 --> 14:25.447
Ae-sun, start with the pot.
Wash the pot first.

14:25.531 --> 14:28.534
Oh. What? What is that woman doing?

14:42.715 --> 14:44.383
Here are some damn yellow croakers!

14:45.885 --> 14:47.887
What is the meaning of this?
Have you gone nuts?

14:47.970 --> 14:49.388
How dare you come in here and--

14:49.471 --> 14:50.598
Money's tight, huh?

14:50.681 --> 14:53.183
-Wh… wh… what?
-You can't afford to feed my little girl?

14:53.767 --> 14:57.146
And you, mother-in-law,
isn't she a daughter of the Oh family?

14:57.229 --> 14:59.857
Are you so surprised
that she takes after her father?

15:00.774 --> 15:02.276
It's not just wrong.

15:02.359 --> 15:03.235
It's mad!

15:04.236 --> 15:05.446
Your dear son!

15:05.529 --> 15:07.031
Your eldest brother!

15:07.531 --> 15:09.450
Right now, he's turning in his grave!

15:09.533 --> 15:11.368
I can see why
he couldn't survive your marriage.

15:11.452 --> 15:13.746
How dare you come here
and blather about my brother!

15:17.499 --> 15:20.169
You must be possessed by a demon
or God-knows-what.

15:21.337 --> 15:23.547
You blame me for my husband's death,
is that it?

15:24.381 --> 15:25.925
Don't you feel sorry for her?

15:26.550 --> 15:28.010
The girl who lost her father?

15:31.138 --> 15:34.058
That's it. I'm taking my daughter now.

15:37.603 --> 15:39.688
Damn you, making her do your dishes.

15:40.773 --> 15:42.066
How dare you!

16:00.292 --> 16:04.296
I'm glad they never gave me any croaker
'cause I get to live with you now.

16:05.547 --> 16:07.091
You like me that much, huh?

16:10.970 --> 16:12.137
What's my secret?

16:12.221 --> 16:13.472
You're my mom.

16:14.098 --> 16:14.932
Goodness.

16:15.808 --> 16:17.559
I like you because you're my mom.

16:17.643 --> 16:19.103
Why would you ask that?

16:19.687 --> 16:20.938
You like me so much?

16:21.438 --> 16:22.439
Better grow up.

16:23.399 --> 16:24.525
'Cause every day,

16:25.651 --> 16:27.528
I'll be expecting my hundred won.

16:28.278 --> 16:29.613
You read my poem!

16:39.373 --> 16:40.541
"Damn Abalones"

16:40.624 --> 16:43.627
written by Oh Ae-sun,
third grade, class eight.

16:44.211 --> 16:46.964
All day, every day, abalones, abalones

16:47.047 --> 16:49.842
When the typhoon blows, abalones, abalones

16:49.925 --> 16:52.636
Worth more than a daughter
Those damn abalones

16:52.720 --> 16:56.098
"Hurry back," I tell her
When she dives in the sea

16:56.181 --> 16:58.726
What could down there
So cold and so deep be?

16:59.435 --> 17:02.229
Is she looking for clams
Buried under the sand?

17:02.312 --> 17:04.898
Did she run out of breath?
Will she come back to land?

17:04.982 --> 17:07.234
Why does a daughter
Wait here on the shore?

17:07.317 --> 17:10.362
Because damn abalones
That's what it's all for

17:13.282 --> 17:15.909
If abalones cost a hundred won to find

17:15.993 --> 17:18.579
I'd pay it all back
For a day of Mom's time

17:19.496 --> 17:21.081
My mom with her sore back

17:21.582 --> 17:23.208
My mom with her bad cough

17:24.501 --> 17:28.088
A hundred won per day
If it means my mom can rest

17:39.391 --> 17:42.603
Did you ever hear of such a daughter
who can write like this?

17:44.271 --> 17:45.939
How did I get so lucky?

17:54.114 --> 17:55.574
Told you so.

18:11.632 --> 18:15.135
Give me 100 won every single day,
and I won't have to dive.

18:18.013 --> 18:18.931
That way,

18:19.598 --> 18:21.892
I'll have all day
to spend with my daughter.

18:23.644 --> 18:25.354
You see why it was second place?

18:25.437 --> 18:27.189
Judges must have been blind.

18:28.023 --> 18:29.024
You didn't like it?

18:29.108 --> 18:30.818
They only gave it second place?

18:31.610 --> 18:32.986
They should've made it first!

18:52.673 --> 18:53.882
Don't mistreat her.

18:53.966 --> 18:56.510
If you do,
your ass will be out on the street.

18:56.593 --> 19:00.764
My dear, you have no luck with husbands,
but your children are another story.

19:01.598 --> 19:03.016
Oh, this little brat.

19:03.684 --> 19:05.269
The worst brat of all brats.

19:06.478 --> 19:07.729
Still a pain in the ass.

19:07.813 --> 19:10.440
I'd take a brat like that
any day of the week.

19:14.695 --> 19:17.447
My father and mother
were up to their ears in debt.

19:17.948 --> 19:19.658
My first husband was bedridden.

19:20.492 --> 19:22.369
And my second husband's a deadbeat.

19:22.452 --> 19:25.330
I've accepted it.
It was my destiny to bear all that weight.

19:25.414 --> 19:28.250
All anyone did was
climb onto my back to be carried.

19:30.169 --> 19:31.420
This tiny thing.

19:32.588 --> 19:34.006
She keeps climbing down.

19:35.132 --> 19:37.718
She keeps asking
to share some of the burden.

19:42.389 --> 19:44.183
And that makes her a brat, um,

19:45.392 --> 19:48.270
because that's the thing
that breaks my heart more than anything.

19:48.353 --> 19:50.564
Just you wait.

19:50.647 --> 19:54.359
That brat will be taking care of you
long into the afterlife.

19:54.443 --> 19:58.822
My goodness. I'm a worthless mother
who wouldn't even dare to dream.

20:02.367 --> 20:03.577
I can't leave her yet.

20:04.203 --> 20:05.621
I wanna be around

20:06.413 --> 20:09.958
to see the day
when the world praises her as a scholar.

20:12.336 --> 20:15.464
She'll be the next Han Seok-bong one day,
mark my words.

20:16.173 --> 20:17.466
Our Ae-sun.

20:18.508 --> 20:21.220
If any of us can make
something of our lives, it's her.

20:27.392 --> 20:29.519
THE FIFTH NATIONAL ASSEMBLY ELECTION

20:33.857 --> 20:37.486
Oh my, do you realize that,
thanks to you, I have a new title now?

20:38.820 --> 20:41.823
You, being VP of your class,
makes me a VP's mother.

20:41.907 --> 20:43.533
Let's celebrate with rice cakes.

20:43.617 --> 20:46.328
Who said
I wanted to be vice president?

20:46.411 --> 20:47.996
The whole fishing industry is like that.

20:48.080 --> 20:50.666
Behind every captain
is a vice captain ready to lead.

20:50.749 --> 20:53.669
If everyone's on top,
then who's vice president?

20:53.752 --> 20:56.255
The second-in-command has more influence.

20:56.338 --> 20:59.508
Who would wanna be second-in-command?

20:59.591 --> 21:01.635
I've never even been a hall monitor.

21:01.718 --> 21:05.430
I want "Ae-sun, voted vice president"
written in the family history book.

21:05.514 --> 21:08.642
Don't write that down.
Don't you dare write that down!

21:08.725 --> 21:11.395
You know, I thought Oh Ae-sun
was actually voted president.

21:11.478 --> 21:13.563
Uh-huh, I'm sure she was.

21:13.647 --> 21:16.400
You just make sure to serve
your president well, then.

21:16.483 --> 21:20.195
Ae-sun got 37 votes,
Lee Man-ki only got 28.

21:20.279 --> 21:22.197
So why is Lee Man-ki class president?

21:22.281 --> 21:24.199
Why do I have to be vice president?

21:24.283 --> 21:26.201
My presidency was stolen!

21:26.785 --> 21:27.828
"It was stolen"?

21:28.328 --> 21:31.331
CLASS PRESIDENT ELECTION
OH AE-SUN, LEE MAN-KI

21:31.832 --> 21:34.334
Don't you think
you're being a little selfish here?

21:34.418 --> 21:36.837
I don't get it. I got 37 votes.

21:39.089 --> 21:41.341
Honestly, you have some nerve, young lady.

21:42.801 --> 21:45.846
Didn't you eat the cream buns
Man-ki's father handed out?

21:47.139 --> 21:50.726
And haven't we all enjoyed the floors
waxed with the candles he gave us?

21:52.185 --> 21:54.521
But I still got 37 votes.

21:56.982 --> 21:59.443
I say it was unethical of them
to not vote for Man-ki

21:59.526 --> 22:01.069
after taking the stuff he gave them.

22:02.237 --> 22:04.656
A real leader needs to have it all. Eh?

22:04.740 --> 22:07.868
Both the material aspect,
as well as the moral.

22:07.951 --> 22:08.785
You know?

22:09.494 --> 22:11.079
But I got 37 votes.

22:11.163 --> 22:14.708
Who cares how many votes you got?
You may as well have a hundred!

22:14.791 --> 22:15.792
Because in the real world,

22:15.876 --> 22:18.128
it doesn't matter a bit
who gets more votes!

22:18.211 --> 22:19.838
I'm sorry, but between you and Man-ki,

22:21.048 --> 22:24.843
there's a certain something
that just matters more. Understand?

22:30.223 --> 22:32.351
It'll be embarrassing for you
to get kicked out.

22:32.434 --> 22:33.810
There's no shame in just resigning.

22:34.436 --> 22:35.812
It's for the greater good.

22:36.396 --> 22:38.148
Sometimes you have to lose to win.

22:41.068 --> 22:43.195
A loser is still a loser.

22:43.278 --> 22:46.114
And nothing I do will change that!

22:46.198 --> 22:47.699
Why is this happening to me?

22:47.783 --> 22:49.034
It's not fair!

22:49.117 --> 22:50.410
Oh, cut it out!

22:50.494 --> 22:52.287
Why are you chasing that crap?

22:52.371 --> 22:54.748
Look at the posters of the men
running for office.

22:54.831 --> 22:56.875
They're all going bankrupt for nothing.

22:56.958 --> 22:58.877
But the presidency is mine!

22:59.461 --> 23:01.880
Give me back my presidency!

23:24.945 --> 23:27.572
After that fit you threw,
I thought you'd never come see us again.

23:27.656 --> 23:30.325
You know, if I'm being completely honest,

23:30.867 --> 23:33.036
your household needs a rude awakening.

23:33.120 --> 23:35.205
Did they want a daughter-in-law or a cow?

23:35.288 --> 23:37.833
I mean, really, how the hell
are you gonna plow this field?

23:37.916 --> 23:39.042
Well, I can't pay you.

23:43.505 --> 23:45.715
Uh, will you just go? Go on!

23:46.216 --> 23:48.677
My mother-in-law
would kill me if she found out.

23:49.261 --> 23:51.555
Besides, you can just run away.

23:51.638 --> 23:54.391
I'm afraid my ghost will be
haunting that family forever.

23:54.474 --> 23:57.269
I can plow this for you
and get all the sesame as well.

23:57.352 --> 23:58.937
I swear, I can't pay.

24:00.397 --> 24:02.858
What, you don't believe me? Just look.

24:02.941 --> 24:03.859
I have nothing.

24:03.942 --> 24:07.070
Yes, you do. You know what I mean?

24:08.113 --> 24:10.574
-Huh?
-Do whatever you want with me.

24:10.657 --> 24:12.868
Nothing will change the fact
that I'm penniless, okay?

24:12.951 --> 24:15.370
Please. I don't want cash.

24:16.288 --> 24:18.331
I'm after the… thing.

24:18.832 --> 24:19.666
Uh…

24:20.375 --> 24:22.419
Y… Y… You know.

24:25.589 --> 24:27.007
No way. Impossible.

24:27.924 --> 24:29.634
Why not? Why not?

24:29.718 --> 24:33.054
I'll plow the whole field for you.
And harvest all the rest too.

24:33.138 --> 24:35.265
I'm doing all this.
You could at least let me borrow it.

24:35.348 --> 24:38.351
There's no way in hell.
I don't even wear it. It's so pricey.

24:40.061 --> 24:43.773
Listen, in just two days,
I'll plow this entire field.

24:43.857 --> 24:47.110
We can pretend you borrowed a cow
or something, all right?

24:50.697 --> 24:53.241
Come on.
Who lends their wedding jewelry out?

24:53.325 --> 24:55.744
You should have asked for something
when you remarried.

24:56.244 --> 24:59.164
Don't you know me by now?
I work harder than a cow.

25:27.067 --> 25:28.109
STUPID ABALONE

25:28.193 --> 25:30.529
THE LOYAL LEE FAMILY
BY LEE MAN-KI FROM CLASS 3-8

25:32.072 --> 25:34.491
A loyal family. Yeah, right.

25:34.574 --> 25:36.368
You think a child wrote this?

25:36.451 --> 25:38.703
Obviously,
the parents did the whole thing.

25:40.664 --> 25:41.498
Hey.

25:42.332 --> 25:43.333
Come look at these.

25:43.416 --> 25:45.919
This one is clearly the best, hmm?

25:47.128 --> 25:48.838
Who cares about the gold frame?

25:48.922 --> 25:51.800
This one here is much better written.
Don't you agree?

25:52.551 --> 25:54.511
Well, I see.

25:55.053 --> 25:57.514
The general's son's always first, hmm?

25:57.597 --> 25:59.849
The general's son
gets to be class president?

25:59.933 --> 26:02.519
We all have to bow down
to the general's son?

26:02.602 --> 26:04.729
Ho-ho! We'll see about that!

26:05.855 --> 26:07.232
Excuse me, ma'am?

26:07.899 --> 26:09.192
Are you Ae-sun's aunt?

26:12.571 --> 26:14.447
-Please, have a seat.
-Thank you.

26:23.164 --> 26:25.000
MASTERMIND OF THE 3.15 ELECTION FRAUD

26:32.465 --> 26:36.219
So… I'm not Ae-sun's aunt.

26:36.928 --> 26:37.971
I'm her mother.

26:38.972 --> 26:40.849
Oh, oh. Oh, of course.

26:41.391 --> 26:43.810
She's always had a mom, just so you know.

26:44.436 --> 26:45.604
Yes, right.

26:46.187 --> 26:47.689
I was so busy making a living,

26:48.356 --> 26:50.191
I never had the chance to visit you.

26:51.443 --> 26:54.654
I brought along some rice cakes
for you to share with the students.

26:55.739 --> 26:57.282
Hmm, you shouldn't have.

26:58.825 --> 27:00.869
Actually, I brought these for a reason.

27:03.705 --> 27:06.958
My daughter is
a very "presidential" vice president.

27:10.420 --> 27:12.881
She's also a first-place,
second-place winner.

27:17.010 --> 27:19.554
What did my teacher say?
Did he admit I won?

27:19.638 --> 27:21.264
Did he say I could be president again?

27:23.683 --> 27:25.018
You got angry, didn't you?

27:25.101 --> 27:27.479
Did you make a scene
like you did at Grandma's place?

27:27.979 --> 27:29.689
I made a scene, all right.

27:29.773 --> 27:31.900
He'll think twice
before opening his mouth.

27:33.777 --> 27:36.446
Yes, well, the students and I
will enjoy these…

27:36.529 --> 27:38.740
Uh, my child is in your care,

27:39.407 --> 27:41.826
and… and I'm just trying
to make a decent living.

27:41.910 --> 27:45.080
Of course.
I have 70 students in this class.

27:46.122 --> 27:48.541
They're always so hungry,
as you can imagine.

27:48.625 --> 27:51.836
So I'm not sure this will be enough
to share with everyone.

27:52.629 --> 27:55.757
Well, I'm sure that all their parents
feel the same way I do.

27:57.008 --> 27:58.134
Please, if you would,

27:58.843 --> 28:00.512
take kindly to my daughter.

28:00.595 --> 28:02.639
Does it make a difference
if I take kindly to her?

28:02.722 --> 28:04.349
Every child has to earn it. Hmm.

28:04.849 --> 28:06.976
The rice cakes might not be enough,

28:07.060 --> 28:11.815
but surely, every parent on earth wants
their child to be loved by their teacher.

28:13.692 --> 28:15.110
Uh, if I could have,

28:15.652 --> 28:17.570
I would have brought a cow for you

28:18.113 --> 28:19.322
if I had one.

28:21.408 --> 28:23.076
But I got you these.

28:23.159 --> 28:24.994
Oh, you didn't have to do that.

28:25.078 --> 28:28.331
Ae-sun's teacher should keep
his feet warm. That's what I thought.

28:30.834 --> 28:32.669
Nylon. They're nylon.

28:56.776 --> 28:58.695
She has manners.

29:04.409 --> 29:06.369
That's too much. She shouldn't have.

29:07.120 --> 29:09.664
Did she go out of her way
to stop by the bank?

29:09.748 --> 29:11.166
These are new bills.

29:12.792 --> 29:14.627
Why are you so dressed up?

29:14.711 --> 29:16.963
Because I didn't want
to smell like the sea.

29:17.046 --> 29:19.507
I was always taught
to show my teachers respect,

29:19.591 --> 29:22.594
so I didn't want me
or the rice cakes to smell salty.

29:22.677 --> 29:26.139
Listen to your teacher.
It's the only way to get ahead.

29:26.639 --> 29:28.099
Wouldn't it be great to make a living

29:28.183 --> 29:30.643
sitting at a desk,
writing like your teacher does?

29:31.269 --> 29:33.396
But he's not giving
my presidency back, is he?

29:34.564 --> 29:37.192
He wants you to buy him something,
right? Like a broom?

29:38.693 --> 29:41.279
Well, that's the "material" part, I guess.

29:41.905 --> 29:44.574
You know, I've been thinking,
and vice president is better.

29:45.200 --> 29:47.285
My title might have the word "vice"
in front of it,

29:47.368 --> 29:49.454
but it's basically the same role.

29:49.537 --> 29:53.374
I don't lead the class in the morning bow.
But otherwise, it's the same job.

29:53.458 --> 29:55.710
When Lee Man-ki says, "Attention, bow,"

29:55.794 --> 29:57.670
I say it to myself under my breath.

29:59.380 --> 30:01.090
Honestly, vice president is better.

30:04.552 --> 30:07.889
Ae-sun, your mom is not wealthy,

30:08.389 --> 30:09.849
but you are you, okay?

30:10.683 --> 30:11.893
Don't ever back down.

30:11.976 --> 30:13.061
If you want it,

30:13.770 --> 30:14.979
go and get it.

30:16.815 --> 30:18.399
I won't back down if you won't, Ma.

30:18.483 --> 30:21.820
When I'm all grown up,
you know the first thing I wanna do?

30:29.494 --> 30:30.787
What's gotten into you?

30:31.663 --> 30:32.831
I need to live a long life.

30:33.748 --> 30:36.209
Today, my daughter promised me
that when she grows up,

30:36.918 --> 30:38.711
she'll buy me a pearl necklace.

30:38.795 --> 30:40.588
I can't miss out on that.

30:40.672 --> 30:43.091
Oh boy. In which lifetime?

30:44.008 --> 30:46.094
Children grow up
before you know it.

30:46.594 --> 30:48.847
I'll have my pearl necklace
in the blink of an eye.

30:48.930 --> 30:53.393
It's not just children who grow up fast.
Before you know it, we'll be old too.

30:53.476 --> 30:55.436
I just read it in the news.

30:55.520 --> 30:58.439
The average life expectancy
of Koreans is 52.

30:58.523 --> 30:59.774
I'm gonna beat that.

31:00.275 --> 31:03.403
I'll be 70, enjoying all the rewards
that come with it.

31:03.486 --> 31:05.280
And, you know, once I get there,

31:05.864 --> 31:08.741
the little pain I'm in now,
it'll be laughable.

31:08.825 --> 31:09.993
Just funny.

31:20.253 --> 31:21.963
Hang on, but I didn't quit cigarettes.

31:22.046 --> 31:23.381
You will from today.

31:26.301 --> 31:27.427
Hey!

31:27.927 --> 31:29.721
Very funny. Knock it off.

31:30.221 --> 31:32.307
-Ah, ah, ah…
-You gotta be kidding.

31:45.737 --> 31:47.655
Spring is oh-so-short.

31:48.531 --> 31:50.199
Just as soon as it arrives,

31:50.283 --> 31:52.869
the flower celebration
is over before we know it.

31:57.874 --> 31:59.834
The heartless passage of time.

32:20.271 --> 32:22.023
Will you stop being so damn stubborn?

32:22.106 --> 32:25.902
You can barely hold your breath.
You can't dive anymore.

32:25.985 --> 32:27.695
You can all quit your nagging.

32:27.779 --> 32:30.073
These walls will rot
before I let myself die.

32:30.156 --> 32:33.284
You keep diving with
the smell the blood in your lungs.

32:33.368 --> 32:35.203
You may as well dive with
a coffin on your back.

32:35.286 --> 32:37.747
Death is all the same on land or sea.

32:37.830 --> 32:39.749
Hey. Can't you see the Grim Reaper

32:39.832 --> 32:41.709
standing right outside
your house over there?

32:41.793 --> 32:45.171
He's standing there with his black cloak,
waiting for you.

32:45.254 --> 32:48.591
If you go into the sea, that Grim Reaper
over there will follow you.

32:48.675 --> 32:51.803
He'll peek his head under the waves
and snatch your soul right out of you.

32:51.886 --> 32:55.014
If I was scared of him, I would never
have gone into the water.

32:55.098 --> 32:56.933
Haenyeo's lives are one big gamble.

32:57.016 --> 33:00.311
I've overcome death countless times
in the great blue ocean.

33:02.063 --> 33:04.732
Are you just afraid?
Afraid your children will starve?

33:05.441 --> 33:08.152
Gwang-rye. Haenyeo live and die together.

33:08.236 --> 33:10.279
We'll make sure
you don't go hungry, please.

33:10.363 --> 33:13.449
Enough! I won't die begging.
I'll die making another buck.

33:13.533 --> 33:16.202
I won't stop
until my child has more than I had.

33:16.285 --> 33:17.245
I can't die.

33:17.787 --> 33:19.163
I won't die.

33:19.247 --> 33:21.332
You know why ghosts haunt people?

33:21.416 --> 33:25.837
Your regret will become anguish.
Then obsession will turn you into a ghost.

33:25.920 --> 33:28.256
I'm not afraid of ghosts.
I fear for my children.

33:28.339 --> 33:30.758
I will take everything I can
from the underworld

33:30.842 --> 33:33.386
and give it to my children,
or I will die trying.

33:36.889 --> 33:39.392
Well done.
She can't go diving without those clothes.

33:39.475 --> 33:40.560
That little brat.

33:41.227 --> 33:42.979
I should have never taken her back.

33:50.570 --> 33:53.197
OH AE-SUN IS YANG GWAN-SIK'S WIFE
AE-SUN IS GETTING MARRIED

33:57.493 --> 34:01.414
Am I a beggar?
Do you think I'm a beggar?

34:15.887 --> 34:18.389
You leave my mother alone!

34:18.890 --> 34:21.309
Just please, leave her alone!

34:21.392 --> 34:24.145
What's wrong with you, Dragon King?

34:24.228 --> 34:27.190
Why do you take the lives
of innocent people? Why?

34:30.818 --> 34:33.154
Show her some mercy, please!

34:33.237 --> 34:35.364
You can't do this to her.

34:35.448 --> 34:37.950
You can't do this to her.

34:38.034 --> 34:41.412
My mom worked herself
to the bone her entire life.

34:42.538 --> 34:45.124
She never even got on a plane.

34:45.833 --> 34:47.627
I have to get her a pearl necklace.

34:48.127 --> 34:50.338
I have to put her on a plane!

34:50.421 --> 34:53.466
I was gonna do it all for her!

34:54.050 --> 34:56.636
Why?

34:56.719 --> 34:58.262
Why?

35:01.724 --> 35:03.059
Why?

35:08.481 --> 35:10.108
What's wrong with you?

35:10.191 --> 35:11.818
Are you a ghost or what?

35:11.901 --> 35:14.362
Why aren't you saying anything, Gwan-sik?

35:14.445 --> 35:15.696
What do you want from me?

35:16.197 --> 35:17.657
What? What?

35:18.366 --> 35:19.200
Come here.

35:20.701 --> 35:22.203
-What?
-Come!

35:27.917 --> 35:28.960
Another fish?

35:29.043 --> 35:31.295
You think nobody feeds me except for you?

35:33.506 --> 35:35.633
It's not fish. It's chicken.

35:35.716 --> 35:39.303
We don't share our meat with just
anybody around here, you know?

35:40.596 --> 35:41.681
Are you stupid?

35:42.348 --> 35:43.975
You must be stupid.

35:44.809 --> 35:46.269
Crying makes you hungry.

35:46.769 --> 35:48.521
Do you feel sorry for me?

35:48.604 --> 35:50.606
Is that what all the food is about?

35:51.107 --> 35:53.276
If that were true,
I would've given that to a beggar.

35:55.319 --> 35:57.488
You are always so annoying.

35:58.614 --> 35:59.740
Hey.

36:01.033 --> 36:02.160
I'm your elder.

36:13.504 --> 36:15.464
Even if you brought me beef every day,

36:16.299 --> 36:17.800
we still wouldn't get married.

36:18.301 --> 36:19.343
Who says I want to?

36:37.695 --> 36:39.906
She has to live. She has to.

36:40.990 --> 36:43.534
What will happen
to her poor little children?

36:48.122 --> 36:48.998
Mother.

36:52.126 --> 36:52.960
Mother.

37:01.844 --> 37:03.888
Mother, can we go somewhere together?

37:04.764 --> 37:06.349
I'm a little scared.

37:22.281 --> 37:23.115
What is it?

37:23.866 --> 37:24.700
Sh.

37:27.620 --> 37:29.038
Is that you, Mom?

37:52.895 --> 37:55.940
It's like I'm in Aesop's Fable,
and I found the golden axe.

37:56.440 --> 37:58.442
Hold on, am I the axe?

38:01.237 --> 38:02.697
Are you going somewhere, Mom?

38:03.698 --> 38:05.783
Why didn't you just wait until tomorrow?

38:06.284 --> 38:08.327
If I had, the others would have stolen it.

38:09.203 --> 38:11.330
You could have sold them
for a hundred won.

38:14.125 --> 38:16.419
Feeding you makes it worth a thousand won.

38:26.512 --> 38:27.346
Ae-sun,

38:28.764 --> 38:29.890
if I ever die…

38:32.310 --> 38:33.978
leave this house immediately.

38:34.562 --> 38:37.565
Go to your uncle and beg for your life.

38:38.274 --> 38:40.234
Don't stay here as their housekeeper.

38:42.820 --> 38:44.822
No matter what, go.

38:45.656 --> 38:46.741
Promise me.

38:47.616 --> 38:48.534
Don't…

38:49.327 --> 38:50.328
don't say that.

38:53.706 --> 38:56.917
Stay there until your uncle
gives you away to your husband.

38:57.001 --> 39:00.546
The thought of you walking down
the aisle alone would make me cry.

39:00.629 --> 39:03.466
Why are you telling me this?
You know I can't.

39:05.760 --> 39:07.595
I won't sleep until you promise.

39:08.804 --> 39:09.930
Dad is dead,

39:10.890 --> 39:12.516
and now you're dying too.

39:13.184 --> 39:14.935
Why is everyone dying?

39:16.437 --> 39:18.689
I wish I'd never been born.

39:20.775 --> 39:21.609
Ae-sun.

39:22.568 --> 39:23.944
All parents have to die.

39:24.445 --> 39:25.696
It happens to everyone.

39:26.697 --> 39:28.407
But after our parents are gone,

39:29.200 --> 39:30.534
their children live on.

39:30.618 --> 39:31.869
I know you will too.

39:32.787 --> 39:35.247
There will be days when life is hard.

39:36.916 --> 39:38.959
Once in a while, there may be days

39:39.043 --> 39:41.379
when you feel like
giving up on life altogether.

39:41.462 --> 39:43.547
Stop. Stop talking like that.

39:44.131 --> 39:45.383
I won't promise you.

39:45.466 --> 39:47.676
I won't eat the abalone.

39:54.141 --> 39:55.851
Oh, my little girl.

39:57.436 --> 39:58.854
When will you understand?

40:01.982 --> 40:04.985
The eldest daughter,
listening to her mother's dying wish,

40:05.069 --> 40:06.612
was only ten years old.

40:07.571 --> 40:12.660
♪ Sleep, sleep, sleep well ♪

40:13.285 --> 40:18.374
♪ Sleep, sleep, sleep well ♪

40:18.457 --> 40:23.838
♪ Sleep well, darling baby ♪

40:24.338 --> 40:29.301
♪ Sleep well, sleep soon ♪

40:31.095 --> 40:36.058
♪ Black dog, go over yonder ♪

40:36.559 --> 40:40.896
♪ Black dog, go over yonder ♪

40:42.690 --> 40:47.278
♪ Help my baby sleep well ♪

40:47.987 --> 40:52.741
♪ I'll help your babies sleep well ♪

40:54.618 --> 40:56.620
♪ Sleep, sleep… ♪

40:56.704 --> 40:59.832
The mother who left three children behind…

41:01.041 --> 41:03.502
♪ Sleep well, darling… ♪

41:03.586 --> 41:05.379
…was but 29 herself.

41:06.964 --> 41:12.261
♪ Sleep, sleep, sleep well ♪

41:39.872 --> 41:41.749
Crying makes you hungry.

41:41.832 --> 41:43.250
Eat while you cry.

41:49.173 --> 41:51.217
What am I going to do now?

41:52.843 --> 41:53.928
I don't know.

41:55.721 --> 41:56.805
This morning…

41:58.807 --> 42:01.644
my mom died, and now she's gone.

42:03.145 --> 42:04.188
I know she's gone.

42:05.814 --> 42:07.191
But the thing is…

42:12.321 --> 42:14.823
…I miss her so much already.

42:16.742 --> 42:19.537
I already miss her so much.

42:21.664 --> 42:23.165
Oh, Mom!

42:23.249 --> 42:26.210
Oh, Mom, I miss you so much.

42:30.339 --> 42:31.549
Mom!

42:35.678 --> 42:36.804
Mom!

42:43.227 --> 42:46.647
Ae-sun, Sun-nam, Sun-bong.

42:47.231 --> 42:49.441
All your names have a "sun" in them.

42:49.942 --> 42:51.735
That makes you a family.

42:53.362 --> 42:56.699
Just look at you. Even a stray dog
wouldn't wanna marry you.

42:57.908 --> 43:00.327
You know,
it's yellowtail season right now.

43:00.411 --> 43:03.330
I should be on a boat
trying to feed your younger siblings.

43:07.543 --> 43:10.546
You'll just end up being a housekeeper
at your uncle's house.

43:11.130 --> 43:13.716
Honestly, if you'll be one either way,

43:13.799 --> 43:16.719
wouldn't you rather be a housekeeper
for your own siblings?

43:16.802 --> 43:18.220
I won't be a housekeeper.

43:19.805 --> 43:21.599
Mom told me not to live like that.

43:22.141 --> 43:23.601
Ae-sun.

43:24.310 --> 43:27.271
Your mom didn't want your siblings
to live as beggars on the street.

43:29.732 --> 43:32.109
Just stay until yellowtail season is over.

43:33.193 --> 43:34.028
Hmm?

43:34.820 --> 43:37.072
Why don't you use
this good piece of land?

43:37.156 --> 43:38.866
Are you just gonna let it rot?

43:50.210 --> 43:53.672
Just stay
until Sun-bong is potty-trained, hmm?

44:09.271 --> 44:12.524
Just stay until Sun-nam
goes to elementary school. Okay?

44:15.778 --> 44:17.237
Just you wait.

44:17.321 --> 44:19.657
When the color
on your fingernails has faded,

44:19.740 --> 44:22.284
you'll be through with grief
and ready to live.

44:27.539 --> 44:28.749
I know you will.

44:29.249 --> 44:31.043
The days will keep coming,

44:31.627 --> 44:33.712
just as your fingernails keep growing.

44:33.796 --> 44:36.006
Soon enough, you'll forget.

44:36.090 --> 44:38.967
Look here. I made this.
Do you like it?

44:39.510 --> 44:43.305
Your family is bankrupt, isn't it?
Where do you get those fish every day?

44:53.065 --> 44:53.982
Here you go.

44:56.527 --> 44:57.361
Right there.

44:58.862 --> 44:59.863
Look at this.

45:02.991 --> 45:04.368
Isn't it pretty?

45:09.665 --> 45:10.874
I'm moving out.

45:10.958 --> 45:11.917
POEMS OF YU CHI-HWAN

45:15.170 --> 45:17.464
One last boat trip. Huh?

45:18.799 --> 45:22.010
Just a few more deep-sea fishing trips
and I'll have a lifeline.

45:23.804 --> 45:26.223
Other kids get tutoring and time to study.

45:26.306 --> 45:29.601
I tend to the field and make food.
I wanna be first in the class too.

45:29.685 --> 45:31.603
I just-- I just wanna…

45:34.648 --> 45:35.983
Never mind.

45:39.778 --> 45:41.363
Korean literature, right?

45:41.447 --> 45:43.449
Isn't that what you wanna study?

45:43.991 --> 45:45.534
No, poetry! Poetry!

45:46.118 --> 45:48.412
Ae-sun, you said
you'd become a poet. Didn't you?

45:48.495 --> 45:51.290
Poets sure are great.
Aren't they? Like these.

45:54.585 --> 45:58.797
Yi Sang, Kim So-wol, Yun Dong-ju.
They all studied Korean literature.

45:59.298 --> 46:01.425
"If you can't stand the sight of me,

46:01.508 --> 46:02.634
when you leave,

46:03.135 --> 46:05.804
tread lightly but firmly
on your way past."

46:06.764 --> 46:08.390
Help me to pave the way,

46:09.349 --> 46:12.936
and you'll be studying Korean literature
before you know it, hmm?

46:17.316 --> 46:20.944
If you think about it, who paid for
all your schooling so far, Ae-sun?

46:21.028 --> 46:22.571
I'm not just any stepfather.

46:22.654 --> 46:26.742
In fact, I'm practically your real father
at this point. Huh?

46:26.825 --> 46:29.620
Help me make money
and send you to that damn college.

46:30.537 --> 46:31.538
Hmm.

46:32.039 --> 46:34.291
Your uncle wouldn't have sent you
to college anyway.

46:35.209 --> 46:37.795
If that household was gonna
take care of you, they would have--

46:37.878 --> 46:40.631
On the mainland? A mainland school?

46:41.632 --> 46:43.634
Mainland. College on the mainland.

46:43.717 --> 46:45.761
You swear on your children's names?

46:47.304 --> 46:48.972
I swear on my wife's name!

46:49.056 --> 46:52.768
If I forgot the things you've done for us,
your mom would haunt me forever.

46:54.186 --> 46:57.481
The movement to wear simple clothing
continues to be promoted in pursuit of

46:57.564 --> 47:00.484
a more convenient and practical lifestyle
for the people.

47:00.567 --> 47:02.986
When you're at your busiest
and need to hurry,

47:03.070 --> 47:06.782
wearing long skirts can be cumbersome
and extremely uncomfortable.

47:06.865 --> 47:08.784
The aim of this movement is to improve

47:08.867 --> 47:11.870
such impractical aspects
of our daily lives.

47:11.954 --> 47:15.374
For women everywhere,
our nation must be united in this effort.

47:15.457 --> 47:17.334
SPY DETECTION CAMPAIGN PERIOD

47:27.344 --> 47:29.012
ICE

47:55.664 --> 47:56.623
YANG GWAN-SIK

47:57.958 --> 48:00.752
-Would you like one?
-No, I'm here to buy a cabbage.

48:01.461 --> 48:03.714
I know. Would you like a cabbage?

48:05.215 --> 48:06.842
You're selling these cabbages?

48:06.925 --> 48:08.552
They're, uh, very good.

48:10.429 --> 48:11.263
Her cabbages.

48:11.847 --> 48:12.681
They're good.

48:16.059 --> 48:17.311
Come on, everybody!

48:18.020 --> 48:20.105
Fresh fish straight out of the ocean.

48:20.188 --> 48:22.316
It doesn't get any fresher than this!

48:22.399 --> 48:24.902
Haenyeo! Haenyeo!
Haenyeo caught these fish!

48:24.985 --> 48:28.155
Get your sea squirt here.
Abalone, extra fresh!

48:28.238 --> 48:29.615
I'll give you a deal.

48:29.698 --> 48:32.993
Why worry about Gwang-rye's daughter?
She has Steelheart by her side.

48:37.956 --> 48:39.875
My goodness.

49:05.359 --> 49:07.277
Would you like a cabbage? They're good.

49:07.361 --> 49:08.820
Would you like a cabbage?

49:08.904 --> 49:12.157
Gwan-sik sells
all of Ae-sun's cabbages for her.

49:12.240 --> 49:15.786
In today's top trends, women are
fearlessly shortening skirt lengths.

49:15.869 --> 49:17.829
The cabbage is good.
Would you like one?

49:17.913 --> 49:20.207
In Myeong-dong, Seoul,
it's becoming common to see

49:20.290 --> 49:23.502
women confidently walking around
with their thighs fully exposed.

49:23.585 --> 49:26.838
Well, you know,
it wouldn't be wrong to say that

49:26.922 --> 49:29.299
Gwan-sik is raising Ae-sun by himself.

49:31.426 --> 49:33.679
Things have reached
the point where there are calls

49:33.762 --> 49:36.556
to crack down on the trend
and reinstate long skirts.

49:36.640 --> 49:39.559
They tell us to wear short clothes,
and now they're complaining about it?

49:39.643 --> 49:41.061
In this broadcaster's opinion,

49:41.144 --> 49:44.356
this is just a distraction from
the real problems this country is facing.

49:44.439 --> 49:45.857
Would you like a cabbage?

49:46.608 --> 49:49.736
The cabbage is good.
Everything over there is good.

49:50.237 --> 49:52.030
They're all good to you,
I'm sure.

49:52.114 --> 49:55.701
Gye-ok, you've got some explaining to do
about that son of yours, eh?

49:56.201 --> 49:57.411
Oh, lucky me.

49:58.578 --> 50:01.707
-So how much is the cabbage?
-One for 50 won. Three for 150.

50:01.790 --> 50:03.333
Huh, that's not fair.

50:03.417 --> 50:06.962
It's perfectly fair for three cabbages
to be 150 if one is 50.

50:08.296 --> 50:09.381
OH AE-SUN

50:09.464 --> 50:10.799
It's just math, you know.

50:11.299 --> 50:13.927
Look, miss.
I didn't ask you how to buy my cabbages.

50:14.011 --> 50:15.804
I want one, not three.

50:16.680 --> 50:19.558
Well, lady, I don't make much
selling cabbages as it is,

50:19.641 --> 50:20.934
and everyone wants a lower price.

50:21.935 --> 50:23.270
I beat them to the punch this way.

50:23.353 --> 50:25.605
Who wants to be punched
for doing their shopping? My gosh.

50:27.149 --> 50:28.525
-All right.
-There he goes.

50:29.109 --> 50:31.486
-One it is.
-Saves her yet again.

50:31.570 --> 50:32.946
I gave birth to a dumbass.

50:33.989 --> 50:36.033
I only want one, okay? That's it.

50:38.326 --> 50:40.996
Sometimes, I wonder if that girl
has hands of her own.

50:41.079 --> 50:42.247
I'm not forcing him.

50:42.748 --> 50:44.583
He does it because he wants to.

50:44.666 --> 50:46.043
No one's making me do a thing.

50:48.170 --> 50:49.171
Oh God.

50:49.254 --> 50:51.131
Should've raised a stray dog instead.

50:51.631 --> 50:52.466
Better watch out.

50:52.549 --> 50:55.260
Your grandma will kill you
if she catches you together again.

50:55.343 --> 50:57.679
At that age,
they think they're invincible.

50:57.763 --> 50:59.848
You think they're afraid of an old lady?

51:02.225 --> 51:03.727
Chicken! My chicken!

51:03.810 --> 51:04.936
Oh no.

51:09.733 --> 51:10.567
Wait!

51:11.318 --> 51:12.319
Out of my way!

51:12.402 --> 51:13.278
Grandma!

51:13.361 --> 51:14.362
Oh!

51:16.865 --> 51:20.494
How many times have I told you
not to set up shop next to that girl?

51:20.577 --> 51:22.662
Why do you keep coming
all the way out here?

51:22.746 --> 51:25.665
Haven't you heard that daughters
take after their mothers? Huh?

51:25.749 --> 51:27.417
I can't believe you let a girl

51:27.501 --> 51:30.295
who has her mother's ghost following her
be near your baby.

51:30.378 --> 51:32.047
Wake up!

51:32.130 --> 51:33.507
That grandma needs Jesus.

51:33.590 --> 51:35.467
I take after my dad, thank you very much!

51:35.550 --> 51:37.177
Ah, you little brat, Ae-sun!

51:37.260 --> 51:38.804
-Come back here, Ae-sun!
-Whoa, whoa!

51:38.887 --> 51:40.806
-Damn you, girl!
-What did I do?

51:40.889 --> 51:42.599
I told your grandson no!

51:43.350 --> 51:45.936
-I said, "No, thank you." All right?
-Move aside.

51:46.019 --> 51:49.147
-Just wait till I get my hands on you!
-Please, Mom. Let it go!

52:03.578 --> 52:06.581
But no matter how many times
I said "No, thank you,"

52:06.665 --> 52:09.042
eventually, there would be no going back.

54:54.332 --> 54:59.337
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS."
